Only raw frame bytes are reproduced (as test fixtures), not tcpdump's own C
dissector source, none of which was read or ported. The implementation under
test (`lldp.zig`/`cdp.zig`/`arp.zig`/`dhcp.zig`) is the authors' own
clean-room work from the public IEEE/RFC specifications, as the root `NOTICE`
§2 `l2disco` entry and this module's README "Provenance" note already record;
these captures anchor that implementation against genuine wire bytes,
including — for several of the LLDP fixtures — the exact byte sequences that
are publicly documented (by the fixture's own file name in the upstream
project) to have broken another independent implementation's dissector for
the same protocol.
